Title: Same name, new place
Author: tsukuri
Speed: 1.1

/* Original text written for tsukuri release 1. The narration is read by a synthetic voice. */

# Two screens

= A box on one screen and a box on the next: is it the same box?

INT. TITLE CARD - DAY

Same name, new place {#title @mc .title}
A small idea about moving boxes {#sub @bc .muted}

NARRATOR
(slowly)
Here is a small idea about moving things.

NARRATOR
A box can glide across a screen only if we know it is the same box.

INT. FIRST SCREEN - DAY

First screen {#tag @tl .label}
A box {#box @ml .box}
Another box {#twin @mr .box hidden}

NARRATOR
Picture a box on a screen. [[focus: box]]

NARRATOR
On the next screen there is a box too. [[next]] Is it the same box, or a new one?

# A name that stays

= Give every box a name, and each screen can follow it.

> CUT

INT. THE NAMES - DAY

Box one {#one @ml .box}
Box two {#two @mr .box}
Every box has a name {#tag @tc .label}

NARRATOR
Give every box a name. [[focus: tag]] Here the names are one and two.

> AUTO-ANIMATE

INT. THE NEXT SCREEN - DAY

Box one {#one @mc .box}
Every box has a name {#tag @tc .accent}
Same name, so it moves {#hint @bc .muted}

NARRATOR
[[sfx: whoosh]] On the next screen, box one sits somewhere else. Its name matches, so it slides there.

/* INTERIM WORKAROUND, not a creative choice: at the story rate (1.1) whisper.cpp hears "has" as "is" in the next Line and the exact-match ratio falls to 0.875, below 0.9. At 1.05 it is heard correctly. Remove this (speed 1.05) once word timings come from the synthesizer or the alignment is judged by its path (follow-up to spec 0001). */
NARRATOR
(speed 1.05)
Box two has no match, so it leaves.

> AUTO-ANIMATE

INT. A NEW NAME - DAY

Box one {#one @mr .box}
Same name, so it moves {#hint @bc .accent}
Box three {#three @ml .box}

NARRATOR
[[sfx: ding]] A name we have not seen before is a new box, so it appears.

INT. THREE ANSWERS - DAY

Three answers {#head @tc .title}
Same name: it moves {#same @ml .box}
New name: it appears {#new @mc .box hidden}
Missing name: it leaves {#gone @mr .box hidden}

NARRATOR
Comparing two screens by name gives three answers.

NARRATOR
The same name means it moves.

NARRATOR
A new name means it appears. [[next]] A missing name means it leaves. [[next]]

INT. THE POINT - DAY

Same name, new place {#title @mc .title}
Keep the name and the motion comes free {#sub @bc .muted}

NARRATOR
(pause 0.5)
So keep the name, and the motion comes for free.
